# Detectors & Data Sync Rule

Whenever a **new detector** or **dataset** is added to the backend (or removed/renamed), the UI registry and its tests **must** be updated in lockstep.

## Files to update

1. **`src/components/waste/waste-detectors-data.tsx`**
   - Add/remove the entry in `DETECTOR_GROUPS` (for detectors) or `DATASETS` (for datasets).
   - Set `isNew: true` on any newly added detector or dataset.
   - Keep the ordering consistent: detectors grouped by category, datasets in logical order.

2. **`src/components/waste/waste-detectors-data.test.tsx`**
   - Update the expected-count constants at the top of the file:
     - `EXPECTED_DETECTOR_GROUPS` — number of category groups
     - `EXPECTED_TOTAL_DETECTORS` — total detector count across all groups
     - `EXPECTED_TOTAL_DATASETS` — total dataset count
   - If a new Socrata dataset ID is added, add it to `EXPECTED_SOCRATA_IDS`.
   - If a new detector group (category) is added, verify the group-level tests still pass.

## Checklist for adding a detector

- [ ] Add entry to the correct group in `DETECTOR_GROUPS` with `id`, `name`, `description`, and `isNew: true`
- [ ] Increment `EXPECTED_TOTAL_DETECTORS` in the test file
- [ ] Run `npm run test` and verify all tests pass

## Checklist for adding a dataset

- [ ] Add entry to `DATASETS` with `id`, `socrataId`, `name`, `description`, and `isNew: true`
- [ ] Add the Socrata ID to `EXPECTED_SOCRATA_IDS` in the test file
- [ ] Increment `EXPECTED_TOTAL_DATASETS` in the test file
- [ ] Run `npm run test` and verify all tests pass

## Checklist for adding a detector group (new category)

- [ ] Add the new group object to `DETECTOR_GROUPS`
- [ ] Increment `EXPECTED_DETECTOR_GROUPS` in the test file
- [ ] Increment `EXPECTED_TOTAL_DETECTORS` by the number of detectors in the new group
- [ ] Run `npm run test` and verify all tests pass
